WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.038
Step ten breaks it on purpose.

2
00:00:02.038 --> 00:00:05.701
Append one line to the packaged
summary, and verify again.

3
00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:09.238
It exits one: the summary
doesn't match its hash.

4
00:00:09.238 --> 00:00:12.776
Then try to package day one
as if it came after day two,

5
00:00:12.776 --> 00:00:14.751
chained to day two's manifest.

6
00:00:14.751 --> 00:00:19.162
It exits one too: this run isn't
later than the previous package.

7
00:00:19.162 --> 00:00:22.849
So an edited file and a swapped
package are both refused,

8
00:00:22.849 --> 00:00:27.175
and that's what lets the ISSO trust
the chain without trusting you.

9
00:00:27.175 --> 00:00:32.438
The step ends by linting the scheduled
workflow, with no findings and no warnings.

10
00:00:32.438 --> 00:00:37.626
Step eleven runs the tests in both folders:
five hundred thirteen Pester tests pass

11
00:00:37.626 --> 00:00:42.588
in PowerShell, and one hundred forty-two
pytest tests pass in the drift pipeline.

12
00:00:42.588 --> 00:00:45.340
Then delete the output
folder in both places.
